<title>PHILIPPINES: Some Jardine Fleming staff move to M. Lynch.</title>
<headline>Some Jardine Fleming staff move to M. Lynch.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Top officials and research staff of Jardine Fleming's Philippine stockbroking arm have quit to join Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Inc, a Jardine Fleming spokesman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Between eight and 10 staff of Jardine Fleming Exchange Capital Securities Inc, including chairman Rene Ongpin and managing director Jojo Madrid, quit the company, a Jardine Fleming spokesman said by phone from Hong Kong.</p>
<p>&quot;We are anxious to maintain our leading position in the equities market in the Philippines,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;We will be looking to building our staff within the Philippines,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Jardine Fleming has sent some of its best researchers to back up its Manila unit while it scouts for a new team, he said.</p>
<p>Jardine Fleming is 50 percent owned by Jardine Matheson Holdings Ltd.</p>
<p>Merrill Lynch was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
